      <title>Secure Communications with Jabber</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Internet Services</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In this talk, Peter Saint-Andre will discuss the existing security features of Jabber technologies and how they are being extended to ensure complete privacy of communication over the Internet.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When you chat with a friend in your living room or a colleague in your office, you expect the conversation to be private. Unfortunately, your online conversations may not be private -- it all depends on what technology you use.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There are many reasons why Jabber is more secure than existing IM and presence technologies, so Peter will explain those and how they help prevent spam on the Jabber network.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;He will also talk about the Intermediate Certification Authority that Jabber recently launched to issue free digital certificates for Jabber servers.&#xA;Finally he will talk about the end-to-end encryption technology they are developing for complete privacy of instant messaging.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
